  "stem": "The expression \\((2x - 3)^{2} - 4x(x - 5)\\) is equivalent to \\(ax + b\\), where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are constants. What is the value of \\(a\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "8"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Expand the square: \\((2x - 3)^{2} = 4x^{2} - 12x + 9\\).",
    "Expand the product: \\(4x(x - 5) = 4x^{2} - 20x\\).",
    "Subtract: \\(4x^{2} - 12x + 9 - 4x^{2} + 20x = 8x + 9\\), so \\(a = 8\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\np = Poly(expand((2*x - 3)**2 - 4*x*(x - 5)), x)\nassert p.degree() == 1\nassert p.coeff_monomial(x) == 8\nassert [Rational(v) for v in spr_answers] == [8]",
